  "body": "## What changed\n\nThis PR adds tests only. The new binary `crates/app/tests/tilted_gouge_kinds.rs` audits each operation kind that accepts a tilt.\n\n- Each probe cuts into a correct box part (a synthetic mesh with 12 facets) in a box stock on the 4th-axis mill (`tormach-770mx-microarc4.mch`).\n- Each probe runs at A 90 and at A -90. Each probe also runs upright as a guard, except 2D Adaptive. Each pose has its own world.\n- The test asserts three things:\n  - a blocking verdict at generation (`Warning::Gouge`, or `Warning::StockChamferGouge` for the 2D Chamfer);\n  - a refused post (`post blocked`, and `cuts past the finish surface` when the op is tilted);\n  - no file is written.\n\nThe decision entry is `docs/decisions/2720-tilted-gouge-audit.md`.\n\n## Results\n\n| Kind | Probe | Test | Result |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Face | stock source, cut 1 mm under the part skin | `a_tilted_face_into_the_part_is_refused` | refused |\n| Contour | whole part, Outside, a second part 2 mm past the wall along X | `a_tilted_contour_into_a_neighbour_part_is_refused` | refused |\n| Pocket | whole part, area offset 3 mm into the part | `a_tilted_pocket_offset_into_the_part_is_refused` | refused |\n| 2D Adaptive | whole part, area offset 3 mm into the part | `a_tilted_adaptive_offset_into_the_part_is_refused` (A 90), `a_tilted_adaptive_offset_into_the_part_is_refused_at_a_minus_90` | refused |\n| 2D Offset | whole part, area offset 3 mm into the part | `a_tilted_offset2d_offset_into_the_part_is_refused` | refused |\n| Engrave | whole part, 7 mm deep on a 3 mm mark budget | `a_tilted_engrave_deeper_than_a_mark_is_refused` | refused |\n| Trace | whole part, 7 mm deep on a 3 mm mark budget | `a_tilted_trace_deeper_than_a_mark_is_refused` | refused |\n| 2D Chamfer | stock source, the part fills the stock | `a_tilted_chamfer_of_the_stock_into_the_part_is_refused` | refused (`StockChamferGouge`) |\n| Circular | stock source, cut 1 mm under the part skin | `a_tilted_circular_into_the_part_is_refused` | refused |\n| Slot | - | `tilted_gouge.rs` (#2600), not repeated | refused |\n\nNo kind posts a tilted gouge, so this PR files no P1.\n\n## Where a tilted gouge cannot be expressed\n\n- **Contour into its own part:** the app refuses this at create. Side Inside on a whole section is refused (\"needs picked rings\"). A negative stock to leave is refused (\"not usable\"). Thus the probe uses a neighbour part. The gap is along X, the tilt axis, so the neighbour stays beside the wall in each pose.\n- **2D Chamfer on a part source:** this has no depth law by design, because the chamfer must break the part edge. Thus only the stock-source chamfer (#1631) can express a gouge.\n\n## Readings\n\n- Quick gate `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main` on 678f3a37e: 1 step, 0 failed. `app suites: tilted_gouge_kinds` is ok in 52 s (10 passed, 0 ignored).\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- B rotation, compound A+B tilts, and `basis_version` 0. All probes use `basis_version` 1, B 0, A 90 or -90.\n- Tilts that are not a quarter turn (for example A 30).\n- Upright 2D Adaptive: in debug it takes more than 60 s, and the keep law suite (#1603) covers it.\n- Picked-ring (Selection) sources. All probes use the whole part or the stock.\n- TrochoidalSlot, Probe and PlasmaProfile: they have no tilt.\n- Observation: a 2D Adaptive with `optimal_load` 0.5 on this fixture ran for more than 9 minutes in debug. I stopped it. I did not measure it in release. Filed as #2736.\n\nThe stale comments near `params.rs:1365` and `sane.rs:112` are not in touched lines, so this PR does not change them.\n\nChangelog: none\nEffort: high\n\nFixes #2720\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n\n",
